nused edge on the U-side path to a via Find(U[i]); if depth[Find(U[i])] > depth[a], we can use edge Id edgeIdChild[Find(U[i])]. Otherwise, try the V-side similarly. If an edge is found, output a line with endpoints of that T1 edge (A[e], B[e]) and endpoints of the T2 edge (U[i], V[i]). Ensure each T1 edge and each T2 edge is used at most once by the DSU rules.\n- Print the total number of matches and all quadruples (a_i, b_i, c_i, d_i).\nThis approach handles n up to 250k within time limits and memory constraints.\n",
